How to run:

1) Event Parsing from json
    Access the event_reading file 
        cd event_reading
    Run the python script thats in the event_reader.py. Needs 1 argument which is the json file.
        python3 event_reader.py ../matches/16010.json >> results.txt

2) Run the thread per client server
    Compile using make command
    Run the server 
        ./server -s [speed] -n [number of clients] -p [port] -f [parsed events file] (The position of the arguments doesn't matter)
    Run the viewer
        ./viewer -p [port] -h [hostname]

3) Tests
    Compile using make command
    Run the server with one client and a big speed for the test to run in a short amount of time
        ex ./server -s 10000 -n 1 -p [port] -f [parsed events file]
    Run the test
        make test

4) Pitch view
    Compile using make command
    Run the server 
        ./server -s [speed] -n [number of clients] -p [port] -f [parsed events file] (The position of the arguments doesn't matter)
    Run the pitchview script
        python3 pitchview.py [localhost] [port] (For now the arguments need this specific order)

